 "note": [
  "Every KJV epigraph is replaced by the verbatim Louis Segond (1910) text with the (KJV) tag dropped, and the attribution swaps the KJV sentence for the Segond sentence used by a-retrospect-teens.fr. The 2 Corinthians 12:9 epigraph starts at « Ma grâce te suffit » (the English's “And he said unto me” is omitted), and Psalm 77:7-9 is cited in Segond numbering as Psaume 77:8-10, without its « — Pause. »",
  "Bunyan's own sentences are rendered freshly into a slightly elevated French, not taken from any published French translation. The “My grace is sufficient” / “for thee” device is recast: the fragment that came first is « Ma grâce suffit », and the missing piece is the little word « te » (« à toi »). The sermon's “My love” (Song of Solomon 4:1) is « Mon amour » / « Tu es mon amour », not Segond's « mon amie », and Ecclesiasticus 2:10 (not in Segond) is self-rendered.",
  "Names and terms: the game of “cat” is « le jeu du bâtonnet »; Francis Spira appears under his Italian name, Francesco Spiera; Ranters and Bedlam are kept with a gloss; OCD is « TOC »; “counsellor” is « psychologue »; “half a mile” is « quelque huit cents mètres ». The two books from the wife's dowry keep their English titles in italics with a French gloss. The original title is given as « La grâce abondante envers le premier des pécheurs », and The Pilgrim's Progress as « Le Voyage du pèlerin », as on the site.",
  "As in a-retrospect-teens.fr, narration uses the passé simple and the reader is addressed as « tu ». The book title « La grâce abondante (Pour ados) » is 31 characters long, which is over the usual 28. AI-translated in-session; awaiting native review."
 ],
